<.page_shell flash={@flash}>
  <.legal_page eyebrow="Privacy" title="Request data deletion" updated="31 July 2026">
    <p class="text-ink-muted text-lead font-light">
      You can ask Nila, operated by Kaguya Media Private Limited, to delete or
      anonymise personal data associated with you or your business. This includes
      eligible account details, WhatsApp communications and metadata, uploaded
      documents, and records derived from them.
    </p>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">How to make a request</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Email
        <.text_link
          href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax?subject=Data%20deletion%20request"
          class="font-medium"
        >
          privacy@nila.tax
        </.text_link>
        from your registered business email with the subject “Data deletion
        request”. Include your name, company or firm name, registered email, and
        the phone number associated with the WhatsApp communications you want
        deleted. Do not send identity documents unless we ask for them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">What happens next</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We will acknowledge the request, verify that you are authorised to make
        it, and identify the relevant data. We will then delete or anonymise
        eligible data and confirm when the request is complete. If the data
        belongs to one of our customers' clients, we may coordinate with that
        customer before acting on the request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Data we may retain</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Some records may be retained where required by legal and regulatory
        retention requirements, to establish or defend legal claims, prevent
        fraud or abuse, or preserve necessary security and audit records. We
        restrict retained data to those purposes and delete it when the applicable
        retention period ends. Residual copies in protected backups expire through
        the normal backup lifecycle.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        For questions about deletion or any other privacy right, contact <.text_link
          href="mailto:privacy@nila.tax"
          class="font-medium"
        >
          privacy@nila.tax
        </.text_link>.
        Our broader handling practices are described in the <.text_link
          navigate={~p"/privacy"}
          class="font-medium"
        >
          privacy policy
        </.text_link>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </.legal_page>
</.page_shell>
